e lead went straight back to +12.1."}, {"turn": 37, "text": "With Black at +13.4, E6 filled the hole in Black's own wall and lost 25.5 points, leaving the score at -12.1. The engine wanted D2, a move into White's weak bottom-left. White's G1 then regained 26.6 points."}, {"turn": 43, "text": "Black led +15.0 when B5 cost 27.0 points, and the lead became -12.0. The 10k's A7 was the biggest slip of White's game at 28.5 points, and it put Black back at +16.4. The engine's choice for both sides was A2, the same corner point."}, {"turn": 45, "text": "H8 was the worst move of the game, losing 34.4 points and turning +16.4 into -17.9. The engine's choice was A2, the point that had mattered for the last several moves. White's A3 afterwards lost only 4.2 points, and Black never got back into the game."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py only flood-fills groups and lists their liberties on a pasted board, count.py only tallies stones and enclosed empty regions for the current position, and the games.md commands only read or append notes. None of them generates, scores or ranks candidate moves or looks ahead at any continuation.", "stop": false}}